 the one that's happening today, and here I am, in Sierra, with some cool people.Solar eclipses happen rarely enough, and frequently enough, to act as milestones in my life: I can review what happened since the previous one, and make a plan for the next one.They are some of the most magnificent natural phenomena, much more interesting than what's expected.The only other one that I got to see in perfect conditions was in my home town, Isfahan in 1999. I hope this one is perfectly clear again, and I have some resolutions for the next one.replyembedding-shape 51 minutes ago | prev | next [–] This is great, can easily see what spots are overfilled with people or not :) I'm still thinking about where exactly I'll go to see it, was thinking Calafell or Vilanova as they're nearby and easily accessible, but probably half of Barcelona thinks the same so better to go a bit inland. Probably I'll end up just outside Lleida I think.Any more Spanish HNers (or temporary visitors) who are going to any specific places to see it? :)replyegesko 1 minute ago | parent | next [–] I'm in Valencia, planning to watch it from the beach.replyAl-Khwarizmi 13 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'm from A Coruña so I should be able to just go down to the street, walk like 100 m and see it. I just hope clouds don't spoil the show (at the moment it's looking good, but here you never know).replyiancuandrei 27 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'll go somewhere around Bilbaoreplydavidricodias 40 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] Colmenar Viejo seems a great spot ;)replyembedding-shape 35 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] Only 7 hours away :D I'm in the Maresme area, so probably will end up between València and Tarragona on some mountain :) Thanks for the tip though, I'll forward it to my Madrid friends.replyhagen8 30 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] Mountains close to leon?replyNKosmatos 12 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Thanks for posting this, most of us won’t be able to view the eclipse but having a few webcams really helps to get the feeling!Hoping to be able to see the great eclipse of 2027 live ;-)https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2027-august-2replyTornhoof 30 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sierra de Guadarrama - Puerto de Cotos https://www.infonieve.es/espacio-nordico/puerto-de-cotos/web... looks decent, different views, good weather.replyxanthine 37 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sorry for my ignorance, but can someone please explain what I'm looking at here?replymsdz 34 minutes ago | parent | next [–] About five hours from now, the sections of Europe indicated on the map will experience a total solar eclipse, with other regions of the continent experiencing a partial one.The map shows feeds to watch it.replyembedding-shape 35 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] Today there is a eclipse, the map shows where the eclipse will be. In the path of the eclipse, there are also a ton of live webcams, and this map shows those and let you preview the webcams. Does it make sense now?replyrob74 21 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] Even more specifically, it will start off over Greenland, continue over western Iceland and then finish with the sunset in northeastern Spain and the Balearic Islands.replyvoidUpdate 14 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] If you pan to the right, it shows that it actually starts in a bit of russiareplyLawrenceKerr 21 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Doesn't seem like the best of weather now in Iceland, hopefully it clears up. Otherwise it would suck for the people who have planned the trip months if not years in advance only to get a clouded sky, but that's always the risk with astrotravel.replybenoliver999 17 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Surely the smart money is to go to Spainreplyembedding-shape 13 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] We do get cloudy days too sometimes :) Although today it is looking fairly sunny all over the place: https://i.imgur.com/4LK7xo8.pngreplymatsemann 23 minutes ago | prev | next [–] https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2026-august-12Nice page showing where it will be, with times and visualizations for any point/city.replyMadrasTh0rn 17 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Very coolreply4gotunameagain 32 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Really cool. I'm quite curious as to where the webcam data came from, as it seems to be from various websites/sources.replymoron4hire 28 minutes ago | prev [–] I took my kids out of school and took an unplanned day off work in the middle of an important meeting series to drive 5 hours west from Virginia to Ohio to see the last eclipse. The schools and my boss were both yelling at me, both saying the eclipse wasn't a good enough excuse. I'm sorry, but it definitely was. I am so glad I did that. I would do it again in a heartbeat.replyUncle_Brumpus 7 minutes ago | parent [–] I drove ~3 hours to the Vermont-Canada border... and then drove 14 hours home. I'd also do it again in a heartbeat.I almost signed up for a live-work program for a big music festival happening in Iceland, but the flights (the only thing not covered) were astronomically expensive and I had already made plans with my dad last weekend, and he's getting older so I really didn't want to bail on him.I would love to sit atop the Rock of Gibraltar (with 47,000 other people) for the next one, Aug 2 2027, but that is likely also a pipe-dream, because NORMAL flights to Gibraltar are already too expensive for me.reply Guidelines | FAQ | Lists | API | Security | Legal | Apply to YC | Contact Search:\n=== END PAGE TEXT ===\n\nGoal: Visit Hacker News and:\n1. Identify the top story on the front page (the first article in the list)\n2. Drill into its comments thread\n3. Record the story title (key=story_title) and story URL (key=story_url) in working memory\n4. Record your summary of the top 3 comments as key=top_comments (one paragraph, 2-3 sentences)\n5. Call terminate(finalAnswer=...) with a one-paragraph summary including the story title and